  "rules": [
    "Model forecasts exhibit a severe upward bias when the true outcome reverses sharply downward (e.g., Example 2 and 5), failing to account for immediate volatility spikes.",
    "Forecasts systematically underestimate price surges following high sentiment events or recent price peaks, often lagging by 10-15% in the first week of a rally.",
    "When history shows a downward trend followed by a sudden spike (e.g., Example 3), the model defaults to a flat or slow-rising trajectory instead of capturing the momentum.",
    "Sentiment history is largely ignored; even with low sentiment scores, models fail to predict the magnitude of subsequent price jumps seen in Examples 4 and 5.",
    "The model assumes linear growth from the last known price, ignoring the non-linear acceleration observed during market stress periods."
  ]
